    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d442-a1">

                <pb facs="0578" n="510" xml:id="pg510"/>

                <head>Mr. McCulloch to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Treasury Department</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-09-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 24, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your letter of the 25th July last,
                    submitting, for examination of this department, a communication, of the 29th
                    March previous, from Mr. Burlingame, relating to the liberal provisions which
                    had been made by the Chinese authorities for the establishment of lighthouses on
                    their coasts, and requesting any suggestions on the subject which this
                    department might find reason to make, having, with the despatch of Mr.
                    Burlingame, been referred to the Light-house Board, I have the honor to transmit
                    herewith a copy of their report, which embodies the views of this department on
                    the subject. The despatch of Mr. Burlingame, as requested in your communication,
                    is herewith returned.</p>
                <p>I am, very respectfully,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. McCULLOCH, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the
                        Treasury</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, Secretary of
                            State<hi rendition="#italic">.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d442-a1-a1.xml" xpointer="d442-a1-a1"/>
